        "z": "terrain"
      },
      "source": "parcel map",
      "status": "mapped, +/-2 m",
      "notes": "Scenic Brook Plaza, 8313 W US 290, 6.33 ac. It touches our back line directly, with no platted right-of-way or buffer strip between. A ~60 m wide arm runs ~160 m south behind the Candelaria lots."
    },
    {
      "entity_id": "retail_east_end_stormwater",
      "type": "stormwater_area",
      "geometry": { "kind": "polygon", "points_m": [[-3.1, 59.7], [5.9, 8.2], [2.9, 4.8], [-15.6, 1.5], [-18.9, 20.4], [-22.9, 19.7], [-46.5, 42.3], [-47.6, 48.3], [-44.2, 52.6]], "z": "terrain" },
      "source": "retail site plan SP-2019-0411D, Correction #1 (approved Feb 9 2026), sheet OP01, fitted along the tract's east line (our back line)",
      "status": "outline +/-1.5 m (top of bank)",
      "notes": "Detention basin with sedimentation and filtration basins and a pond access road. Top of berm 1,047.0 ft; 100-year water level 1,045.7 ft; basin floors about 1,041-1,043 ft, so a 4-6 ft deep basin, mowed to 18 in or less. Its east berm comes within ~1.5 m (5 ft) of our back line and the basins span the whole line. The live oaks inside it (8-18 in trunks) are marked for removal. Correction #1 adds a lift station (wet well) that pumps out the detention basin. Fit check: the 22.67 ft right-of-way segment lands on our lot's north back corner within 0.1 m."
    },
    {
      "entity_id": "retail_south_arm_woods",
      "type": "woods",
      "geometry": { "kind": "polygon", "points_m": [[-40.1, 0.0], [-157.4, 0.0], [-157.6, 59.7], [-71.2, 59.7], [-51.8, 61.0]], "z": "terrain" },
      "source": "SP-2019-0411D Correction #1: sheets OP01 (layout), EC01 (limits of construction, trees to remain) and TL01 (tree list)",
      "status": "trees to remain (City-approved Feb 9 2026); outline +/-2 m; tree heights not surveyed",
      "notes": "The retail lot's south arm, 196 ft wide, behind the Candelaria lots south of ours. It holds the water-quality spray-irrigation area, with 50 ft irrigation buffers along the Candelaria lots and at its south end. Construction inside it is limited to narrow trench corridors for the irrigation lines; surveyed trees outside them are marked to remain and protected (no parking, driving or storage under them). Mostly live oak with 8-18 in trunks, some cedar elm and Ashe juniper. These woods sit across our back-yard sight lines to the apartments."
    },
    {
      "entity_id": "retail_irrigation_area",
      "type": "stormwater_area",
      "geometry": { "kind": "polygon", "points_m": [[-52.4, 64.0], [-44.2, 20.6], [-141.9, 15.8], [-142.4, 59.6], [-71.2, 59.7]], "z": "terrain" },
      "source": "SP-2019-0411D Correction #1, sheet OP01 ('Water quality irrigation area, 0.98 acre')",
      "status": "outline +/-2 m (traced area 0.98 ac, matching the label)",
      "notes": "Treated runoff from the filtration basin is pumped and sprayed onto the woods here after storms. The soil is Brackett-rock outcrop, design infiltration 0.2 in/hr. The 50 ft buffers keep spray off the Candelaria lots."
    },
